skill from `.github/skills/agentic-workflows/SKILL.md` or \\n- Type `debug the agentic workflow weekly-research failure in https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32951128567`\\n\\n\\n\\n&gt; [!TIP]\\n&gt; \\n&gt; Stop reporting this workflow as a failure\\n&gt;\\n&gt; To stop a workflow from creating failure issues, set `report-failure-as-issue: false` in its frontmatter:\\n&gt; ```yaml\\n&gt; safe-outputs:\\n&gt;   report-failure-as-issue: false\\n&gt; ```\\n&gt;\\n&gt; \\n\\n\\n&gt; Generated from [Weekly Research](https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32951128567) · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Asameerkhansf%2FSameer-Khan+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-id%3A+weekly-research%22&amp;type=issues)\\n&gt; - [x] expires  on Sep 2, 2026, 9:13 AM UTC\\n\\n\\n\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-26T09:13:52Z\",\"labels\":[\"agentic-workflows\"],\"number\":5,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[aw] Weekly Research failed\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-26T09:13:52Z\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-actions\"}},{\"body\":\"This issue tracks all runs where threat detection flagged problems in agentic workflows in this repository. Each workflow run that completes with a detection warning or failure posts a comment here.\\n\\n\\nWhat is a Detection Problem?\\n\\nA detection problem occurs when the threat detection system either:\\n- **Detects potential security threats** (prompt injection, secret leak, malicious patch)\\n- **Fails to produce results** (agent failure, parse error)\\n\\nWhen `continue-on-error: true` (the default), these problems produce warnings and safe outputs still proceed. When `continue-on-error: false`, they block safe outputs entirely.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHow This Helps\\n\\nThis issue helps you:\\n- Track workflows where threat detection raised concerns\\n- Review patterns of detection warnings or failures\\n- Identify false positives or recurring issues with threat detection\\n- Monitor the health of the threat detection system\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nResources\\n\\n- [GitHub Agentic Workflows Documentation](https://github.com/github/gh-aw)\\n\\n\\n\\n&gt; [!TIP]\\n&gt; To configure threat detection behavior, update the frontmatter:\\n&gt; ```yaml\\n&gt; safe-outputs:\\n&gt;   threat-detection:\\n&gt;     continue-on-error: true   # Warnings only (default)\\n&gt;     # continue-on-error: false  # Strict mode — block safe outputs\\n&gt; ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n&gt; This issue is automatically managed by GitHub Agentic Workflows. Do not close this issue manually.\\n&gt;\\n&gt; **No action to take** - Do not assign to an agent.\\n\\n\\n\\n&gt; - [x] expires  on Sep 25, 2026, 9:13 AM UTC\",\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-08-26T09:13:49Z\",\"labels\":[\"agentic-workflows\"],\"number\":4,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[aw] Detection Runs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-26T09:13:50Z\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-actions\"}},{\"body\":\"### Workflow Failure\\n\\n**Workflow:** [Weekly Research](https://github.com/githubnext/agentics/blob/ae8d551f07c7ed7619f8c58c7bb4c3ac89395d38/workflows/weekly-research.md)  \\n**Branch:** main  \\n**Run:** https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32950532586\\n\\n\\n&gt; [!WARNING]\\n&gt; **Engine Failure**: The `claude` engine terminated unexpectedly.\\n\\n**Last agent output:**\\n```\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.736Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;github&#34;: Cleared connection cache for reconnection\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.736Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;safeoutputs&#34;: HTTP connection closed after 0s (cleanly)\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.737Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;safeoutputs&#34;: Cleared connection cache for reconnection\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.740Z [DEBUG] LSP server manager shut down successfully\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;github&#34;: HTTP connection dropped after 0s uptime\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;github&#34;: Connection error: SSE stream disconnected: AbortError: The operation was aborted.\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;github&#34;: Terminal connection error 1/3\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;safeoutputs&#34;: HTTP connection dropped after 0s uptime\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;safeoutputs&#34;: Connection error: SSE stream disconnected: AbortError: The operation was aborted.\\n2026-08-26T09:00:35.741Z [DEBUG] MCP server &#34;safeoutputs&#34;: Terminal connection error 1/3\\n```\\n\\n\\n\\n### Action Required\\n\\n**Assign this issue to an agent** to debug and fix the issue.\\n\\n\\n\\nDebug with any coding agent\\n\\nUse this prompt with any coding agent (GitHub Copilot, Claude, Gemini, etc.):\\n\\n````\\nDebug the agentic workflow failure using https://raw.githubusercontent.com/github/gh-aw/main/debug.md\\n\\nThe failed workflow run is at https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32950532586\\n````\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nManually invoke the agent\\n\\nDebug this workflow failure using your favorite Agent CLI and the `agentic-workflows` prompt.\\n\\n- Start your agent\\n- Load the `agentic-workflows` skill from `.github/skills/agentic-workflows/SKILL.md` or \\n- Type `debug the agentic workflow weekly-research failure in https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32950532586`\\n\\n\\n\\n&gt; [!TIP]\\n&gt; \\n&gt; Stop reporting this workflow as a failure\\n&gt;\\n&gt; To stop a workflow from creating failure issues, set `report-failure-as-issue: false` in its frontmatter:\\n&gt; ```yaml\\n&gt; safe-outputs:\\n&gt;   report-failure-as-issue: false\\n&gt; ```\\n&gt;\\n&gt; \\n\\n\\n&gt; Generated from [Weekly Research](https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32950532586) · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Asameerkhansf%2FSameer-Khan+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-id%3A+weekly-research%22&amp;type=issues)\\n&gt; - [x] expires  on Sep 2, 2026, 9:02 AM UTC\\n\\n\\n\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-26T09:02:02Z\",\"labels\":[\"agentic-workflows\"],\"number\":3,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[aw] Weekly Research failed\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-26T09:02:02Z\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-actions\"}},{\"body\":\"### Workflow Failure\\n\\n**Workflow:** [Weekly Research](https://github.com/githubnext/agentics/blob/ae8d551f07c7ed7619f8c58c7bb4c3ac89395d38/workflows/weekly-research.md)  \\n**Branch:** main  \\n**Run:** https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32949965312\\n\\n\\n&gt; [!WARNING]\\n&gt; **Model has no AI credits pricing**: The agent failed because model `openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch` is not in the built-in pricing table and no default fallback pricing is configured. The AWF API proxy rejected every inference request with HTTP 400.\\n\\nThis is a **configuration issue** — retrying will not help. The model must have pricing before the workflow can run.\\n\\n\\nHow to fix this\\n\\n**Option 1 — Add pricing in the workflow frontmatter:**\\n\\n```yaml\\nmodels:\\n  providers:\\n    anthropic:\\n      models:\\n        &#39;openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch&#39;:\\n          cost:\\n            # Placeholder values — replace with actual pricing for this model\\n            input: &#34;0e0&#34;      # $0.00 per million input tokens\\n            output: &#34;0e0&#34;     # $0.00 per million output tokens\\n            cache_read: &#34;0e0&#34;  # $0.00 per million cache-read tokens\\n            cache_write: &#34;0e0&#34; # $0.00 per million cache-write tokens\\n```\\n\\nUse the provider key matching your engine: `github-copilot` (Copilot), `anthropic` (Claude), `openai` (Codex), or `google` (Gemini). Only `input` and `output` are required; the rest default to zero (or `output` for `reasoning`).\\n\\n**Option 2 — Map the model to a known model using the `models` field:**\\n\\nIf `openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch` is an alias for a model already in the built-in pricing table, use the `models` frontmatter field to provide the mapping:\\n\\n```yaml\\nmodels:\\n  &#39;openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch&#39;:\\n    - claude-sonnet-4-5\\n```\\n\\n**Option 3 — Switch to a model already in the built-in pricing table:**\\n\\nReplace `openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch` in the workflow frontmatter with a model name that the AWF pricing system recognizes (e.g. `claude-sonnet-4-5`, `gpt-4.1`, `gemini-2.0-flash`).\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Action Required\\n\\n**Assign this issue to an agent** to debug and fix the issue.\\n\\n\\n\\nDebug with any coding agent\\n\\nUse this prompt with any coding agent (GitHub Copilot, Claude, Gemini, etc.):\\n\\n````\\nDebug the agentic workflow failure using https://raw.githubusercontent.com/github/gh-aw/main/debug.md\\n\\nThe failed workflow run is at https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32949965312\\n````\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nManually invoke the agent\\n\\nDebug this workflow failure using your favorite Agent CLI and the `agentic-workflows` prompt.\\n\\n- Start your agent\\n- Load the `agentic-workflows` skill from `.github/skills/agentic-workflows/SKILL.md` or \\n- Type `debug the agentic workflow weekly-research failure in https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32949965312`\\n\\n\\n\\n&gt; [!TIP]\\n&gt; \\n&gt; Stop reporting this workflow as a failure\\n&gt;\\n&gt; To stop a workflow from creating failure issues, set `report-failure-as-issue: false` in its frontmatter:\\n&gt; ```yaml\\n&gt; safe-outputs:\\n&gt;   report-failure-as-issue: false\\n&gt; ```\\n&gt;\\n&gt; \\n\\n\\n&gt; Generated from [Weekly Research](https://github.com/sameerkhansf/Sameer-Khan/actions/runs/32949965312) · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Asameerkhansf%2FSameer-Khan+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-id%3A+weekly-research%22&amp;type=issues)\\n&gt; - [x] expires  on Sep 2, 2026, 8:55 AM UTC\\n\\n\\n\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-26T08:55:38Z\",\"labels\":[\"agentic-workflows\"],\"number\":2,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"[aw] Weekly Research has no AI credits pricing for model (openai/gpt-3.5-turbo:batch)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-26T08:55:38Z\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-actions\"}}]"
